### 7. Critical Austrian Tax & Regulatory Rules

#### Loss Offsetting Rules (*Verlustausgleich*)

* **Same Tax Bracket (27.5% Pool):** Realized losses from shares, ETFs, and foreign exchange gains can only be offset against income subject to the same 27.5% KESt rate (capital gains, dividends).
* **Restrictions:**
* Capital losses **cannot** be offset against standard bank deposit interest (taxed at 25% KESt) or traditional employment income.
* Losses cannot be carried forward to future calendar years (*Verlustvortrag ist für Privatanleger ausgeschlossen*). All loss offsetting must occur strictly within the same calendar year (Jan 1 – Dec 31).
* *Steuereinfach* brokers handle this loss pool automatically within the calendar year.



#### Deposit & Custody Fees (*Depotgebühren*)

On a €10,000 balance, fixed monthly or percentage custody fees impact net performance:

* Traditional Austrian banks often charge annual custody fees (e.g., 0.15% to 0.30% + VAT, plus minimum quarterly account maintenance fees).
* Discount brokers like **Flatex Austria** charge **€0 depot custody fees** for standard stocks and ETFs (exchange connection fees or third-party venue costs may apply).

